{{- /* chezmoi:modify-template */ -}}
{{- /*

Merge the settings chezmoi owns into whatever is already on disk, instead of
replacing the file.

Claude Code rewrites ~/.claude/settings.json itself — reordering keys, recording
UI state, registering plugins you install from inside a session. A plain
template fought with that: every apply reverted those changes, and anything
deliberately kept out of this public repo (work-only plugins) was stripped.

mergeOverwrite lets the managed side win on the keys it names while leaving every
other key alone. Nested maps merge, so enabledPlugins and extraKnownMarketplaces
gain our entries without losing yours. Arrays are replaced wholesale, which is
what we want for hooks.

Consequence worth knowing: this can add and change keys but never remove one.
Dropping a managed key from the template leaves it in place on machines that
already have it — delete it from ~/.claude/settings.json by hand.

*/ -}}
{{- /* .chezmoi.stdin is absent, not empty, outside an actual apply (chezmoi cat
       and chezmoi status render without it), so test for the key rather than
       its value or the template errors with "map has no entry for key". */ -}}
{{- $current := dict -}}
{{- if hasKey .chezmoi "stdin" -}}
{{-   if trim .chezmoi.stdin -}}
{{-     $current = .chezmoi.stdin | fromJson -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $managed := includeTemplate "claude-settings.json" . | fromJson -}}
{{- mergeOverwrite (deepCopy $current) $managed | toPrettyJson }}
